Mark Healey <die@spammer.die> writes:

> I've not been able to find what the name for the configuration file for
> the RPMed nethack. 

You mention rpm, so I assume you are running on Linux.
The file is called .nethackrc and you put it in your home directory.
Because the game normally runs suid games (at least that's the default
when you compile from source, I don't know if the rpm version is
different), you need to give worldwide read permissions to the file:

chmod a+r ~/.nethackrc

And to be able to find the file, the game must also be able to access your
home directory, so you must give worldwide execute permissions to the
directory: 

chmod a+x ~

